# all-help-no-harm hook environment (dotenvx)
#
# hooks.json wraps the SessionStart, PostCompact, UserPromptSubmit and the
# PostToolUse(AskUserQuestion) recorder hooks in
#   dotenvx run --env-file=${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/.env -- node ...
# dotenvx exits 9 and never runs the hook when this file is missing, so it
# must exist even when it defines nothing.
#
# Optional variables:
#   ANTHROPIC_CONTRACT_LOG_KEY       Anthropic API key of the workspace that holds
#                                    the standing affirmation records (Files API).
#                                    Use a dedicated workspace key: files are
#                                    visible to every key in the workspace.
#                                    Unset: local log only, no server record.
#   ANTHROPIC_CONTRACT_LOG_BASE_URL  Test override (default https://api.anthropic.com).
#
# Provisioning, either way works:
#   1. User environment variable ANTHROPIC_CONTRACT_LOG_KEY (survives plugin
#      updates; existing env vars take precedence over this file).
#   2. Encrypted in this file:
#        dotenvx set ANTHROPIC_CONTRACT_LOG_KEY <key> -f <plugin-root>/.env
#      then put DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY in the user environment. dotenvx writes the
#      private key to .env.keys next to this file; .env.keys is gitignored and
#      must never be committed. The plugin cache is regenerated from the commit
#      on update, so option 1 is the durable choice.
